Parallel Computing Framework:
----------------------------
* During Sabatthical implemented Khronos, a SW implementation of an Out-of-Order (OoO) proccesor. Its a Stack Based Virtual Machine with its own Instruction Set. Instructions are very similar
  to OpenCL kernels and Operands are Tiled Regions of Memory.
* Added DataFlow logic to form an Anti-Dependency Graph from input Instructions and walk the Graph using separate CPU threads to obtain Parallel Execution. 
* Tiles can be Pipelined from Disk right before Instruction execution to minimize Working Set and allow in memory execution.
* Has support for Loops, Branches very similar to Loop Caches in Modern OoO processors. Also has an instruction for Parallel Reduction.
